## ✨ What it does

Your phone's fold animation is a plain cut from one screen to the other. FoldGlass turns it into a moment:

| | |
|---|---|
| 🧊 **The cover frosts over** | The instant the lid starts to lift, the cover screen frosts like a window in winter, while it's still facing you. |
| 🪟 **The swing turns to glass** | When the big screen lights mid-swing, the half that's moving is a sheet of frosted glass, softest at the far edge. |
| 💧 **It clears as it lands** | As the phone flattens, the frost melts away into your live screen. The half in your hand stays sharp the whole time. |
| 🔁 **Closing does it in reverse** | The top half frosts up as it comes down, and the cover lights up frosted and settles into focus. |

<p align="center">
  <img src="docs/images/foldglass-demo.gif" alt="FoldGlass frost clearing" width="300">
  &nbsp;&nbsp;
  <img src="docs/images/fg_frost.png" alt="Frosted" width="250">
