  <img src="docs/images/fg_sharp.png" alt="Clear" width="250">
</p>

### Why it feels real
- **It isn't a blur filter, it's optics.** A custom GPU shader (`fold_glass.agsl`) traces every pixel through a tilted sheet of frosted glass hinged on your fold line. The higher the glass lifts, the softer and darker the picture behind it gets.
- **It follows your actual hinge.** It reads the hinge sensor, learns how fast *you* fold, and uses the gyroscope in the lid to react before the hinge sensor even reports.
- **It plays over any app.** It runs as an Android accessibility service, so it works wherever you are: home screen, YouTube, WhatsApp, anywhere.

---

## 📱 Works on

| Phone | Status |
|---|---|
| **Samsung Galaxy Z Flip 5** | ✅ Built and tested on it |
| Galaxy Z Flip 3 / 4 / 6 / 7, Motorola Razr | 🟡 Same layout (separate cover screen, horizontal hinge). Should work, not tested yet. |
| Galaxy Z Fold, Pixel Fold and other book-style folds | 🟡 Supported in the code (vertical hinge, both halves frost, single-screen switching), not tested yet |

Tried it on another foldable? [Open an issue](../../issues/new) to say how it went. A screen recording helps a lot!

---

## 🚀 Get started (one minute)

1. **Download** `FoldGlass-<version>.apk` from [**Releases**](../../releases/latest) and install it. Allow *Install unknown apps* for your browser if asked.
2. Open **FoldGlass** and tap **Allow** next to *Turn on "FoldGlass" in Accessibility*.
3. In **Settings → Accessibility → Installed apps → FoldGlass**, switch it **on**.
4. Close your phone and open it again. ✨

There's also **Preview here**, to try the effect without folding, and a simpler "fog" version if you'd rather not use accessibility.

---

## 🔒 Privacy

- **No internet permission at all.** FoldGlass physically can't send anything anywhere.
- **Screenshots stay in memory.** It keeps one screenshot of each screen in memory to draw the glass. They are never saved, never shared, and dropped after 15 minutes.
- **Nothing shows on your lock screen.** It never paints a picture of your main screen over the lock screen.
- **It can't read anything.** The accessibility service reads **no** text, no notifications and nothing you type (see [`unfold_accessibility.xml`](app/src/main/res/xml/unfold_accessibility.xml)).

---

## 🛠️ Build it yourself

You need JDK 17 and the Android SDK (platform 35).

```bash
./gradlew assembleDebug
# → app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk
```

## 💜 Credits

The frosted-glass fold idea comes from the "iPhone Duo" foldable concept videos. FoldGlass brings it to real Android phones. It also owes a lot to **[Duo Open](https://github.com/marcoazeem/duo-open)** by marcoazeem, which showed that a system-wide version was possible. See [THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md](THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md).

FoldGlass is an independent project. It is not affiliated with Apple, Samsung, Google or Motorola.

